1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,677
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,860
Believe in what I do.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't wanna live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,657
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,800
We live in wonderland.

26
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,110
Vivi!

27
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:58,860
Who are you?

28
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,420
Ready? Aim!

29
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,120
No, stop it!

30
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,597
Fighting is not going to help anything!

31
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:13,820
I'm fine, Luffy.

32
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:15,274
It only graced my arm.

33
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,190
It's alright.

34
00:02:19,273 --> 00:02:20,220
We won't land.

35
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:22,598
But can you please call us a doctor?

36
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:26,757
Our friend is dying from a
serious illness. I'm begging you.

37
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,240
Please help us!

38
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:30,110
Vivi!

39
00:02:30,193 --> 00:02:33,296
You are not fit to be the
captain of this ship, Luffy.

40
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,774
Not everything can be fixed
by rushing to start a fight.

41
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:41,660
We can't get into a fight here.

42
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Think about Nami.

43
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,631
What would happen to her?

44
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:54,040
Yeah, right.

45
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,560
I'm sorry about that.

46
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,740
Please help us!

47
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:58,940
Call a doctor!

48
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:01,260
Our friend needs you!

49
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:13,740
I'll show you to our village.

50
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:15,780
Follow me.

51
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,697
See, just ask politely.

52
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:28,280
Yeah, you're incredible, Vivi!

53
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,717
There is one thing I feel I
should warn you about, though.

54
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,117
The only doctor we have
here is actually a witch.

55
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,030
Huh?

56
00:03:46,113 --> 00:03:47,040
A witch?

57
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,817
You've got to be kidding me.

58
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,937
Everything about this island is messed up.

59
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:53,844
What do you people call
this weird place anyway?

60
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,817
Actually, this land still
doesn't have a name.

61
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,380
An island without a name?

62
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,562
I didn't know that was possible.

63
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,580
A bear! Hurry, everyone!

64
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,818
Pretend to be dead!

65
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,340
A hiking bear.

66
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,558
He poses no threat.

67
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,396
Don't forget to bow.

68
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:16,836
It's proper manners.

69
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:23,690
Nice.

70
00:04:23,773 --> 00:04:24,778
That's much better.

71
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,957
Now I can finally get back
to some real training.

72
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:35,537
I was getting sick of that modified training
that I had to do with my stupid injury.

73
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:38,561
Besides, just watching the
ship is boring as hell.

74
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:43,842
Maybe some ice water swimming will
help me clear up my head a bit.

75
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,537
This is the village where we live.

76
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,060
Its name is Bighorn.

77
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,657
Look at all the weird animals
walking around everywhere.

78
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,328
Yeah, this is snow country.

79
00:04:57,540 --> 00:05:00,437
Look, Nami, we've made it
to a village with people.

80
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,380
We're here.

81
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:04,305
Thanks for the help, everyone.

82
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:07,597
If you're not a guard, you
can return to your work.

83
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,357
Are you completely certain that
you'll be all right here by yourself?

84
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,520
They are pirates.

85
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,617
I believe these people mean us no harm.

86
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,053
That's my hunch anyway.

87
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:17,751
You can trust me on that.

88
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:19,237
So what should we do now?

89
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,197
If Dalton says they're all right,
then I think we should believe it.

90
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:23,297
They do seem to be pretty harmless, huh?

91
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:24,210
Yeah.

92
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:25,517
All right, Dalton.

93
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,012
We'll leave them to you.

94
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:29,100
Even so, be careful, Dalton.

95
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:31,654
And call us again if you need anything.

96
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:36,577
You mean those men weren't
your land security forces?

97
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:37,490
No.

98
00:05:37,573 --> 00:05:39,037
They're just ordinary citizens.

99
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,591
Come to my house for now.

100
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,630
Hey!

101
00:05:41,713 --> 00:05:42,657
Look over there, Luffy!

102
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:44,057
It's one of those hiking bears!

103
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:44,970
Another one?

104
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:46,037
Hello, Dalton.

105
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:48,297
I heard that some pirates
landed on the island.

106
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:49,877
I hope everything is all right.

107
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:51,313
Yes, everything's fine.

108
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,538
There's nothing to be worried about.

109
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:58,797
Just want you to know, Dalton, I'm looking
forward to the election in two days.

110
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,697
Everyone I've talked to has said
they're going to vote for you.

111
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:03,877
I'm sure you're not serious about that.

112
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,372
I'm just an ordinary citizen, that's all.

113
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:14,457
You can use that bed over there.

114
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,364
I'm going to warm the place up.

115
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:21,737
I guess I should introduce myself.

116
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:22,650
My name is Dalton.

117
00:06:22,733 --> 00:06:25,465
I'm the captain of the
island's security squad.

118
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:28,506
Please forgive our less
than friendly welcome.

119
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:31,257
Excuse me, but may I ask you a question?

120
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:32,170
Huh?

121
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:35,815
It's just that you look
familiar to me for some reason.

122
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:38,960
No, I just have one of
those faces, I guess.

123
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:43,837
Anyway, can you tell us more about this
doctor, or witch, if that's what she is?

124
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,720
Nami's fever's gone up to 107.

125
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,312
How long has she had it?

126
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:51,537
It's been several days, and
it just keeps getting higher.

127
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,450
I see.

128
00:06:52,533 --> 00:06:54,437
She'll likely die if it gets any worse.

129
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,350
Yes.

130
00:06:55,433 --> 00:06:58,617
But we have no idea what the illness
is, much less how to treat it.

131
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:00,077
We don't know how to help her.

132
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,697
We've got to find a doctor
as soon as possible!

133
00:07:02,780 --> 00:07:03,877
Any doctor will do!

134
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:05,217
Where is this witch of yours?

135
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,130
The witch?

136
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,877
Do you see those mountains
outside the window?

137
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,980
Yeah, I noticed them earlier.

138
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:14,295
Supermassive Snowman!

139
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,440
And the feared snowman Snowzilla!

140
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:17,830
Ha ha!

141
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,945
Get in here before I kill you!

142
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:25,477
Those mountains out there are
known as the Drum Rockies.

143
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,460
Look closely.

144
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:30,097
Do you see the castle on top of the
tallest one, the one in the middle?

145
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:31,010
Castle?

146
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,920
That castle has lost its key. Much warmer.

147
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,660
Yeah, I see it up there.

148
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,797
What's so important about the castle?

149
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:42,180
That castle is where our land's
only doctor lives, Dr. Kureha.

150
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:45,249
She's the one who people
here call a witch.

151
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:46,450
What?

152
00:07:46,533 --> 00:07:48,757
Of all places, why does she have
to live on top of a mountain?

153
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:50,697
We need to call her here right now.

154
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:51,956
Nami needs her help.

155
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:55,037
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
there's no way to contact her.

156
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,560
You can't be serious.

157
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:58,457
What kind of a doctor is she?

158
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:01,417
Her skills as a doctor are
quite impressive, actually.

159
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,237
However, she's an eccentric old woman.

160
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:05,580
She's nearly 140 years old now.

161
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:10,777
140 no wonder she doesn't get
around much oh and one more

162
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:14,557
thing she likes pickled plums
what happens when people here get

163
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:17,917
sick or injured doesn't she help
them she comes down from the

164
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,897
mountain whenever she feels like
it she looks around for patients

165
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:24,817
she treats them then before she
leaves she takes whatever she

166
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:27,957
wants from their houses as
payment she doesn't sound like a

167
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:32,177
very nice lady it kind of sounds
like she's a pirate but how is

168
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:35,597
a woman as old as she is capable
of getting down that mountain?

169
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,445
it's an odd rumor around here?

170
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:40,257
several of the villagers
claim they've seen her at

171
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:43,281
night riding a sleigh of
some kind through the sky

172
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:46,067
they see her silhouette
when the moon is out?

173
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:50,265
that's the reason she is
thought to be a witch?

174
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:52,997
there are others who say
they've seen her with a

175
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:56,374
strange creature a creature
that none of them recognize?

176
00:08:56,740 --> 00:09:00,717
See I knew it a snow monster where there's
snow there's gonna be snow monsters.

177
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,271
Oh, I knew there'd be one

178
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,286
I don't want to run into one.

179
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,070
Dr.

180
00:09:09,153 --> 00:09:10,657
Kureha is the only doctor we have,

181
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:13,677
but she's still a woman I
would prefer to stay away from.

182
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:17,697
All we can do is wait for the next time
she decides to come down the mountain.

183
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:18,610
Really?

184
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,000
No, damn it.

185
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:22,097
We can't wait here for that long.

186
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:24,237
Nami is getting even worse as we speak.

187
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,150
Hey, Nami.

188
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:27,000
Nami, wake up now.

189
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,220
Luffy, you idiot!

190
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,849
What are you doing to her?

191
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:33,700
Hey, look, she's awake.

192
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:35,370
Here's the thing.

193
00:09:35,453 --> 00:09:37,637
The only way to see the doctor
is to climb the mountain.

194
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,757
So we're going to have
to climb the mountain.

195
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:40,697
Are you crazy?

196
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:41,610
What about Nami?

197
00:09:41,693 --> 00:09:43,217
How do you expect to get her up there?

198
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:44,937
Easy, she'll ride on my back.

199
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:47,377
That's only going to
make her even more sick.

200
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:48,497
What's the problem?

201
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:50,097
I thought we needed to hurry.

202
00:09:50,180 --> 00:09:52,237
We do, but you'll never make it up there.

203
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,317
Look at how steep and tall that thing is.

204
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,300
I can do it.

205
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:58,737
Maybe you can, but climbing that
thing would be way too hard on Nami.

206
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:01,637
But look, even if we fall or
something, we'll land in snow.

207
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,896
That doesn't matter.

208
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:05,357
A foal like that would
kill even a healthy person.

209
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:08,087
Seriously, Luffy, she
has a really bad fever.

210
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:10,122
It's so high she's almost dying.

211
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:11,829
Don't you understand that?

212
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:20,140
I need to get over this
thing, and quickly.

213
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:25,780
We need to hurry for Vivi.

214
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,460
Come on, Captain.

215
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,330
Let's go.

216
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:38,317
That's what I'm talking about.

217
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,282
Leave it to me.

218
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:43,120
I can't believe this.

219
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:45,888
Now our navigator's as
crazy as our captain.

220
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:48,697
You know, you're in no shape
for a trip like this, Nami.

221
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:49,997
Are you sure you'll be okay?

222
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:51,537
It'll take you hours to get there.

223
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,617
Hey, old guy, give me
some meat for the road.

224
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:54,530
Meat?

225
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:57,180
Right, I'm coming too.

226
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:59,717
Listen, Luffy, be very careful.

227
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,277
You can't fall even once
or Nami is going to die!

228
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,190
Ah!

229
00:11:03,273 --> 00:11:04,103
Not even once!

230
00:11:04,186 --> 00:11:05,137
Hold still a second.

231
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,514
I need to make sure that this is tight.

232
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:10,095
Okay, you're all set.

233
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,637
I'm going to wait for you here.

234
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:14,197
If I came with you guys,
I'd only get in the way.

235
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:15,110
Yep, me too!

236
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,270
Alright.

237
00:11:17,353 --> 00:11:19,447
Now you just hold on
tight to me, okay, Nami?

238
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,467
I guess you're set on going.

239
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:25,437
I'm not going to try to stop you,

240
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:27,737
but I will ask you to at least
climb up from the other side.

241
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:31,114
That way you can avoid the
loppins that are on this side

242
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,459
They're fierce carnivorous rabbits.

243
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:35,097
You run into a pack of them.

244
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:36,077
You're as good as dead.

245
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:36,990
Huh?

246
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,170
Really?

247
00:11:38,253 --> 00:11:39,577
We've got to get up there.

248
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:41,157
We'll be just fine, right?

249
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,300
Yeah, fine.

250
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:46,137
You can't be serious You know how
easily those things can kill you?

251
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:47,397
Nah, we'll be all right.

252
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:50,080
Now hurry it up Sanji before Nami dies!

253
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:53,237
Don't say stuff like that you idiot.

254
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,673
Do you want to Jango us?

255
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,117
Are you sure they'll be all right?

256
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:02,435
Well, it's not really those
two we need to worry about.

257
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:04,157
Nami's the one in trouble.

258
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:06,477
I just hope her strength
can hold out long enough.

259
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,619
She's getting sicker by the minute.

260
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:21,528
Why are you standing there?

261
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:22,960
Come on inside.

262
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:24,338
It's cold out here.

263
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,320
Oh, no, that's really okay.

264
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,540
I want to stay out here. Me too.

265
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:35,350
I see.

266
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,760
Well, in that case, I'll join you.

267
00:12:54,680 --> 00:13:00,637
We did once have some here on this
island you know some doctors however all

268
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:06,997
Of them left some time ago for certain
reasons few months ago we suffered a

269
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:09,037
Vicious attack and our country was

270
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:14,097
destroyed destroyed by pirates oh man The

271
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:19,080
whole country so that's the reason you
acted that way when we showed up yes

272
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:24,220
After the attack the word pirate still
terrifies everyone on this island I'm

273
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,597
sorry about the way we treated you.

274
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,445
Their group was small as well.

275
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:29,980
Only five people.

276
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:32,777
Their captain called himself Blackbeard.

277
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:35,684
Their power was so
incredible they destroyed our

278
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,977
entire country faster
than you would believe.

279
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,531
And there were only five of them fighting?

280
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:42,857
That's impossible.

281
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:43,770
Blackbeard?

282
00:13:43,853 --> 00:13:44,683
What's more,

283
00:13:44,766 --> 00:13:47,337
there are some here who actually believed
that it was good for the country.

284
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,537
What could possibly be
good about that happening?

285
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,450
That's crazy!

286
00:13:50,533 --> 00:13:51,937
Who would Say something like that anyway?

287
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:54,397
Thank you.

288
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,617
I agree.

289
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:57,697
But they have their reasons.

290
00:13:57,780 --> 00:14:01,157
The king who ruled here before
the attack was a horrible man.

291
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:04,260
His rule was despised
by all of the citizens.

292
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:09,711
Our country used to be known as Drum
Kingdom and our king's name was Wobble.

293
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,821
He was the worst king imaginable.

294
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:17,800
Yes, I remember him.

295
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:20,240
I know that man. Not Womple!

296
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:30,617
It feels like it's gotten a little colder.

297
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:32,137
The wind's picking up, too.

298
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:34,697
So why don't you think about
putting on some real shoes?

299
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:36,617
Even seeing your feet
like that is painful.

300
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:37,530
No way!

301
00:14:37,613 --> 00:14:39,340
This is my police. Your police?

302
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:40,837
I think you mean policy.

303
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:41,861
Yeah, that's it.

304
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:45,637
So anyway, though, did you know this?

305
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:48,217
People in snow countries
never sleep at all.

306
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:49,180
Huh? Why?

307
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:51,857
Because if they do,
they'll freeze to death.

308
00:14:51,940 --> 00:14:52,999
Don't be an idiot.

309
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:54,737
Everyone has to sleep sometime.

310
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:55,650
It's the truth.

311
00:14:55,733 --> 00:14:57,562
Someone told me a long time ago.

312
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:00,520
Who, Usa?

313
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:02,955
No, I heard it in a pub in my village.

314
00:15:04,540 --> 00:15:06,097
All right, then explain this.

315
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:08,592
What does that Dalton guy have a bed for?

316
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:10,807
I guess that's a good point.

317
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,500
Hey, maybe it's for when he dies!

318
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:16,999
That's ridiculous!

319
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:20,330
Okay, then.

320
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:21,779
Did you know this?

321
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:25,257
Women in snowy countries have
skin that's as smooth as silk.

322
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:26,170
How come?

323
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:27,340
Isn't it obvious?

324
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:28,717
Here, I'll explain.

325
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:31,437
When you get cold, you rub
your skin to warm it up, right?

326
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,997
It's always freezing cold in
snowy countries like this one.

327
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,077
So the women keep rubbing
their skin all the time.

328
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:38,777
and so it becomes all
white and silky smooth.

329
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,837
Okay, but then how come it's white?

330
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,620
Because the snow,

331
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:46,977
it's constantly falling all over
them, so it dyes their skin all white.

332
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:48,297
Deej, you're really dumb.

333
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:49,317
Did you know that?

334
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:52,518
Yeah, give me a break like
you're really one to talk.

335
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:57,040
You're becoming a pain in my ass! Really?

336
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:58,611
What was with that thing?

337
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,537
Nami, just hang in there
a little bit longer.

338
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:06,208
We're going to get you
to a doctor, alright?

339
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:09,157
Snow's getting really deep around here.

340
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,917
Hey, Luffy, try to run
more smoothly, will you?

341
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,176
You're just making it harder on Nami.

342
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:21,160
What are these things?

343
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:25,440
Well, they're big and they're
white, so they must be polar bears.

344
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:26,810
What's that?

345
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:29,660
You mean you know who Wapol is?

346
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:30,700
Know who he is?

347
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:32,057
We know more than that.

348
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:35,157
He's the pirate who attacked
our ship not too long ago.

349
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:37,057
But I was able to take care of him.

350
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:38,920
Now that I think about it,

351
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:42,077
I do remember him saying something
about heading to Drum Kingdom.

352
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,957
Yes, there's no question about it now.

353
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,257
I remember it clearly.

354
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:48,357
I'm sure I met him once at a monarch
meeting my father took me to.

355
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:51,911
I was still very young then,
but I remember it to this day.

356
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,377
A monarch meeting?

357
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:56,420
Who are you?

358
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:58,920
Oh, no, I, uh...

359
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:02,380
Well, the point is, we do know Wapol.

360
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:05,737
We ran into him yesterday,
when we were on our way here.

361
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:06,650
Yesterday?

362
00:17:06,733 --> 00:17:08,052
Are you sure about that?

363
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,277
But then, I don't understand
what's going on here.

364
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:12,357
He said he was a pirate.

365
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:14,557
He didn't say anything about being a king.

366
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,577
He's just calling himself a
pirate as some kind of disguise.

367
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,957
In truth, Wapol is only
wandering the seas,

368
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,137
trying desperately to
return to this island.

369
00:17:22,220 --> 00:17:23,050
So then,

370
00:17:23,133 --> 00:17:25,497
Wapol and the people who were
on his ship with him were kicked

371
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:28,097
off the island because they
were no match for the pirates?

372
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:29,474
Is that what happened?

373
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:31,820
That's not it. No.

374
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:38,627
When it happened, when we were attacked,
Waple's army didn't even try to fight.

375
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:39,860
In fact,

376
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:42,797
the second he learned how
strong the pirates were,

377
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:45,117
Wapol grabbed his cronies
and ran like a coward.

378
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:48,317
He was the first one to abandon
the country and flee out to sea.

379
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:51,140
After that, the country
felt utter despair.

380
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:53,422
We were left behind by our king.

381
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:56,445
What sort of king would
do that to his country?

382
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,680
A king abandoning his people?

383
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:01,841
Just the thought of that
makes me absolutely sick.

384
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:03,930
Vivi.

385
00:18:04,013 --> 00:18:05,260
You're exactly right.

386
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:07,677
The one good thing that came out of it,

387
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:10,137
though, was the end of
Waple's tyrannical rule.

388
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:12,817
The people who were left on this
island have come together now.

389
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:15,076
We're trying to create a new country.

390
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:19,877
So what we fear most right now is the
return of Wapol and his followers.

391
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:21,725
The return of his brutal rule.

392
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:25,437
We can't afford for him to come
back now with a country so unstable.

393
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:28,237
It would be the end of us we want to build

394
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:31,026
ourselves a new peaceful
nation on this island

395
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:45,897
Seriously, how can it move like that?

396
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:46,837
Is it a gorilla?

397
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:49,540
Oh, it's a polar bear It's a rabbit.

398
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:51,897
How did you go from gorilla to rabbit?

399
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:55,392
These must be the loppins that
Dalton was telling us about

400
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:58,920
Well, there sure are a lot of them.

401
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:05,960
Wubble, come quickly!

402
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:07,580
What is it now?

403
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:10,055
Have you found that pirate's ship yet?

404
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:12,040
No, that isn't it, Wubble.

405
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:14,820
At long last, we've
returned home. We have?

406
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:18,180
How many long months have
passed wandering the sea?

407
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:21,100
That's our homeland, it's Drum Kingdom!

408
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,760
It truly is!

409
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:24,340
I can't believe it!

410
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,460
Listen, Luffy.

411
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:32,680
Let's get going.

412
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:36,940
We have to make it to the castle
where the doctor lives and quickly.

413
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:41,137
I don't want you fighting
these guys, alright?

414
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:42,050
Why not?

415
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:45,336
Because Nami will be able
to feel every move you make.

416
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:47,977
She's too sick to be able to
handle something like that.

417
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:49,295
It would be too much.

418
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,280
She could die.

419
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,190
What?

420
00:19:54,273 --> 00:19:55,103
What?

421
00:19:55,186 --> 00:19:57,669
Jeez, okay, then I
won't fight them at all.

422
00:19:58,340 --> 00:19:59,460
But then...

423
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:02,240
What can I do, huh?

424
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:03,700
Just dodge!

425
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:06,540
Dodge, dodge and run!

426
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,120
But don't retreat!

427
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,929
That's a little difficult!

428
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:13,200
Launcher, shoot!

429
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,090
Dodging!

430
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:22,752
Damn, in this snow I can't get my
footing well enough to land a solid kick!

431
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:29,060
You're attacking all at once!

432
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:31,257
Head for the forest!

433
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:32,222
I'll cover you!

434
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:37,010
Go left!

435
00:20:37,093 --> 00:20:37,957
We'll head to the mountains!

436
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:40,097
We need to get rid of them somehow!

437
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:43,797
It would take us hours to fight them
all off, but how do we shake them now?

438
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,797
For bunnies, these guys are tough.

439
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:46,880
We're in trouble.

440
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:49,630
Stop it!

441
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:54,138
What are you doing?

442
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,377
I told you not to attack, you idiot.

443
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:58,460
Just leave them to me. Sorry.

444
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,955
This is no time to be screwing around.

445
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:03,340
Sanji, we can go up from here.

446
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:04,580
Right, go on.

447
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,340
Wanna give me a lift?

448
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,940
Did you really have to taunt them? Sorry.

449
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:19,962
Run for the top of the mountain.

450
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:23,909
The snow's really
starting to pick up, huh?

451
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,940
Nami, please just be okay.

452
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:29,420
Hello, Dalton!

453
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:31,660
I was looking for you.

454
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:32,697
Bow to the bear.

455
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:33,937
What can I do for you?

456
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:36,377
I heard the newcomers were looking for Dr.

457
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:37,290
Kureha.

458
00:21:37,373 --> 00:21:40,037
Yes, but the sick woman's friends have
already taken her up the mountain.

459
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:44,179
Oh, that's too bad, because I heard
the doctor's in Kokoro right now.

460
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:46,770
She's where?

461
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:48,350
Huh?

462
00:21:48,433 --> 00:21:50,480
Tsunami and the other's already past her?!

463
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:57,840
Come on.

464
00:21:58,020 --> 00:22:00,373
We've had enough of this crying already.

465
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:01,840
Just make him stop.

466
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,420
It's driving me nuts.

467
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:05,380
Yes, I'm sorry.

468
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:07,697
Hey, Tamachibi, what's wrong?

469
00:22:07,780 --> 00:22:08,898
You hurt somewhere?

470
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:12,942
You need to stop crying
and tell me what's wrong.

471
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,765
You're upsetting the customer.

472
00:22:16,360 --> 00:22:17,831
Tamachibi, say something.

473
00:22:17,980 --> 00:22:21,392
If you don't stop crying,
you're going to go to your room.

474
00:22:21,760 --> 00:22:22,642
It's the witch.

475
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:24,240
I can't find the witch.

476
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,080
And look at that.

477
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:28,848
She's got that weird
monster with her again.

478
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:33,350
That's it.

479
00:22:33,433 --> 00:22:35,500
I've had enough of this. Well, well.

480
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:38,157
Doesn't sound like a very
nice father in there.

481
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:40,477
If a child is crying uncontrollably,

482
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,854
Chances are something is wrong
and he doesn't know what.

483
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:48,260
Stay there for now, Chopper.

484
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:54,460
So sorry about that.

485
00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:56,100
It's... you.

486
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:58,960
So are you kids happy?

487
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:04,960
Doctor! Karoo!

488
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:06,937
Anyone want my secret to staying young?

489
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:08,297
No, we're fine, thank you!

490
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:11,300
I can't believe she's
really 140 years old.

491
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:14,340
I'll have you know I'm only 139.

492
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:20,120
Shall I treat the boy?
Wait, what? He's fine.

493
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:23,011
He isn't sick or hurt or anything, really.

494
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:25,600
Excuse me, doctor.

495
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:29,340
Let's go, chopper.

496
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:32,220
Wait, please come back.

497
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,480
I'm sorry.

498
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:38,020
This is my mistake.

499
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:41,137
I was aware that the doctor had come into

500
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:43,117
town from the mountain
in the last few days,

501
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:46,377
but I assumed that she'd left and
wouldn't be back for quite some time.

502
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:47,577
Don't worry about it.

503
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:48,877
This isn't your fault.

504
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:52,297
The problem here is how abnormally
strong Lupi and Sanji are.

505
00:23:52,380 --> 00:23:54,197
Even if we go up the mountain after them,

506
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:56,557
there's no way we'd be
able to catch up to them.

507
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:59,257
If we are able to find the
witch in this Kokoa-wee place,

508
00:23:59,340 --> 00:24:04,217
we just need to tell her to get back up the
mountain as quickly as she possibly can.

509
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:05,880
You're right. That's true.

510
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:07,692
We have no other choice.

511
00:24:08,540 --> 00:24:12,617
Forgive us, forgive this land
for not having more doctors.

512
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:16,717
Don't say that this isn't something
that you need to be apologizing for.

513
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:18,397
Dalton, she's right about that.

514
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:20,700
Let's hurry.

515
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:33,800
It's my hands.

516
00:24:34,500 --> 00:24:36,260
They hurt. Your hands?

517
00:24:36,660 --> 00:24:37,680
All right.

518
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:39,200
How's this?

519
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:41,860
You see?

520
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:44,497
Now you've forgotten all
about your hands hurting.

521
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:45,457
What was that about?

